%% Navigation at scale (J-002): the app refuses a view that would not fit and offers ways out; it never takes one on its own (FR-023, FR-047, PD-031).
flowchart TD
  F[Author sets filters] --> V0{Which view?}
  V0 -- layers --> W{Fit scale at least 0.85?}
  V0 -- matrix --> WM{Matrix fits the free width?}
  W -- yes --> V[Layer view at Fit]
  WM -- yes --> MX[Matrix view]
  W -- no --> M[Message: the view would not fit, with three choices]
  WM -- no --> M
  M -- narrower filters --> F
  M -- focus on a concept --> P[Author picks a concept; from the matrix this opens the layer view, FR-047]
  P --> X[Focus: only its neighbourhood is drawn, FR-045]
  M -- group by domain --> GW{Grouped view fits with every group closed?}
  GW -- yes --> G[Grouped layer view: one group per first-listed domain per plate, BR-009]
  GW -- no --> M2[Message: offers focus or narrower filters only]
  M2 -- narrower filters --> F
  M2 -- focus on a concept --> P
  G -- open a group --> OF{Fits with only this group open?}
  OF -- yes --> O[The open group closes; this group shows its concepts and relations in place, FR-048, FR-049]
  OF -- no --> OM[Group stays closed; message offers focus on one of its concepts or narrower filters, FR-049]
  OM -- focus on a concept --> P
  OM -- narrower filters --> F
  O -- close it --> G
  X -- leave focus --> F
  G -- leave grouping --> F
  V -- Ctrl K finder over the whole store --> S[Chosen concept becomes the selection and is brought into view; filters that hide it are cleared, FR-043]
  MX -- Ctrl K finder over the whole store --> S
  V -- choose a type in the legend --> L[That relation type stays prominent, others recede; with a selection, only its neighbourhood of that type, FR-044]
  L -- choose it again --> V
